Subject: [PATCH 02/51] =?UTF-8?q?begonia=20(MT6785):=20conninfra=20diag=5F?=
 =?UTF-8?q?rx=20=E2=80=94=20add=20decisive=20AP-RX=20DMA=20write-pointer?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20read?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

After a WMT command times out (n=-110), the AP recv consumed nothing, so a
non-zero AP rx-DMA write-pointer (0x11000c00 + VFF_WPT 0x2c) can ONLY mean the
conn replied and the AP DMA captured the frame. This is a mainline-only binary
that splits the bring-up gate without a stock comparison (no consumer ran to
reset the pointer, so no sampling artifact):

  WPT != 0  -> conn replies, DMA captured it; gate is our poll-recv parsing
               (port stock btif_rxd faithfully).
  WPT == 0  -> conn never replied (confirm RX EN live + conn-side TX silent);
               gate is an AP-provided input difference, not an AP-RX bug.

Read-only instrumentation in the existing diag_rx handler (fires per WMT
retry), atomic with the conn-side + AP-TX reads already there. No driver
behaviour change.

Signed-off-by: Michal Andrzejczak <mit.mis@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mtk-conninfra-mt6785.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)
 mode change 100755 => 100644 drivers/soc/mediatek/mtk-conninfra-mt6785.c

diff --git a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mtk-conninfra-mt6785.c b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mtk-conninfra-mt6785.c
old mode 100755
new mode 100644
index 983800d0f..2f12cb1e3
--- a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mtk-conninfra-mt6785.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mtk-conninfra-mt6785.c
@@ -1925,6 +1925,26 @@ static void mtk_conninfra_diag_rx(struct mtk_conninfra *c, const char *label)
 		if (core)
 			iounmap(core);
 	}
+	/* r117 DECISIVE reception-vs-delivery split: AP-RX DMA write-pointer.  The
+	 * recv() just timed out (n=-110), so NOTHING on the AP consumed a reply —
+	 * therefore a non-zero RX WPT can ONLY mean the conn replied and the AP DMA
+	 * captured it (gate = our poll-recv parsing).  WPT==0 with EN live + the
+	 * conn-side TX silent = the conn never replied (gate is an AP-provided input
+	 * difference, not an AP-RX bug).  Mainline-only binary read — no stock
+	 * comparison, so no consumer-resets-the-meter artifact. */
+	{
+		void __iomem *rvff = ioremap(0x11000c00u, 0x80);
+
+		if (rvff)
+			dev_info(c->dev,
+				 "diag_rx[%s] AP-RX: VFF EN=0x%08x WPT=0x%08x RPT=0x%08x VALID=0x%08x ADDR=0x%08x LEN=0x%08x INTBUF=0x%08x\n",
+				 label, readl(rvff + 0x08), readl(rvff + 0x2c),
+				 readl(rvff + 0x30), readl(rvff + 0x3c),
+				 readl(rvff + 0x1c), readl(rvff + 0x24),
+				 readl(rvff + 0x38));
+		if (rvff)
+			iounmap(rvff);
+	}
 }
 
